    "reasoning": "The first cutaway places a separately permeabilized cell boundary around a mitochondrion. The zoom distinguishes its outer and inner membranes, locates cytochrome c between them before release and shows possible passage through the outer membrane into cytosol. The final panel keeps challenge-dependent mitochondrial priming, separately measured intact-cell fate and clinical benefit as three endpoints. This high-level diagram adds the assay compartment and readout missing from the frozen task without introducing an operational protocol or treating priming as measured drug killing.",
